  "body": "## What changed\n\nSeven B-class providers ported from upstream. These consume the model-listing machinery landed in v5.14.2.\n\n| Provider | Model list | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `xai` (Grok) | `/language-models` + `aliases_field` | `REASONING_CONTENT` replay |\n| `together` | `/models` filtered `type=chat` | `reasoning_delta_field=\"reasoning\"` |\n| `deepinfra` | full-URL `/models/list`, `id_field=model_name` | tags→thinking |\n| `siliconflow` | `/models` filtered `sub_type=chat` | |\n| `nebius` | `/models` `verbose=true`, `architecture.modality=text->text` | |\n| `chutes` | `/models` filtered `input/output_modalities=text` + `tools` | |\n| `featherless` | paginated `/models` (`OpenAIModelPagination`) | |\n\nAlso ports the `_MINIMAL_TO_XHIGH` effort tuple (was missing; needed by `nebius`).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full suite: **3942 passed / 6 failed** (6 = pre-existing PowerShell-installer baseline).\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty check`: all clean.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- No live round-trip against any of the seven (no keys available); model listing and request-body construction are tested, the first user with a key is the real smoke test.\n- `featherless` is the first provider to exercise `OpenAIModelPagination` in this fork — its list fetch is covered by the ported machinery tests but not an end-to-end provider round-trip.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
